WEBVTT

00:19.110 --> 00:26.070
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

01:40.980 --> 01:43.480
(One Week After Yuke's Return)

01:43.850 --> 01:48.240
That concludes my report on
our findings in Glad Shi-im.

01:48.240 --> 01:48.520
(Episode 17: The Seven-Leaf Clover)

01:48.520 --> 01:50.260
(Episode 17: The Seven-Leaf Clover)
Well done.

01:50.260 --> 01:53.740
(Episode 17: The Seven-Leaf Clover)
I can't believe you put together
a report like this in just a week.

01:54.110 --> 01:59.020
It's thanks to the help of everyone
in Clover, especially Silk.

01:59.020 --> 02:01.800
No, all I really contributed to the report

02:01.800 --> 02:06.130
was watching him to make sure he
wasn't up all night writing it.

02:06.130 --> 02:07.900
H-Hey!

02:09.220 --> 02:11.760
And here's my report from the academy.

02:12.260 --> 02:14.830
The dimension you and
Niberune traveled through

02:14.830 --> 02:18.100
will be recorded in official
documentation as your discovery.

02:18.100 --> 02:18.810
All right?

02:19.560 --> 02:20.810
Understood.

02:21.560 --> 02:26.340
And as for the matter with Count Crowder
that you brought to our attention...

02:26.340 --> 02:29.570
Marquis Bedibore took care
of that, as well.

02:29.940 --> 02:31.890
What? He did?

02:31.890 --> 02:35.450
I thought a noble should handle
matters of the nobility.

02:35.830 --> 02:39.960
There had been unsavory rumors floating
around about him for some time.

02:39.960 --> 02:42.350
I reported him to the king.

02:42.350 --> 02:42.960
The king?!

02:43.510 --> 02:45.480
Who else would I report it to?

02:45.480 --> 02:48.090
His Majesty listened carefully
to every word.

02:48.440 --> 02:52.340
To the concerns of adventurers as low as us,
who may as well be dirt on his boots?

02:52.700 --> 02:54.530
You are too modest.

02:54.530 --> 03:00.100
Clover is the popular, talented party that
completed this state mission with flying colors.

03:00.510 --> 03:03.930
His Majesty watched your stream
as well, and he liked what he saw.

03:03.930 --> 03:05.960
Well... this is...

03:05.960 --> 03:07.860
I have no words.

03:08.250 --> 03:13.570
We also received official word from Prince
Mastoma, who returned to Salmutaria,

03:13.570 --> 03:18.650
saying that he will see Count Crowder held
accountable for the trouble he caused.

03:18.650 --> 03:20.000
From the prince himself?

03:20.390 --> 03:22.710
With his letter backing the decision,

03:22.710 --> 03:26.750
Count Crowder was placed in
confinement and is awaiting trial.

03:26.750 --> 03:30.290
Between this and the Seeker's Compass,

03:30.290 --> 03:33.340
it looks like we owe Prince
Mastoma another debt.

03:33.340 --> 03:34.970
Actually, about that...

03:34.970 --> 03:37.910
The dungeon in Salmutaria, right?

03:37.910 --> 03:38.890
Yes.

03:39.160 --> 03:43.900
My plan is to conquer the dungeon and
claim it as a personal achievement.

03:44.570 --> 03:48.520
However, there are no true
adventurers in my country.

03:49.030 --> 03:52.220
I think the prince can be trusted.

03:52.220 --> 03:54.530
If Clover can help him out...

03:54.890 --> 03:56.160
Yes, I know.

03:56.590 --> 04:00.150
We will be discussing
what we can do to help.

04:00.150 --> 04:01.290
Is that all right?

04:01.680 --> 04:03.290
I appreciate it.

04:03.680 --> 04:08.650
Lastly, regarding what we will do with
Niberune, the Golden Priestess...

04:08.650 --> 04:11.170
Could you tell me her answer?

04:11.510 --> 04:13.420
Yes. She said...

04:15.820 --> 04:21.850
Duke Bedibore says he's willing to welcome
you as a valued guest from another world.

04:23.480 --> 04:24.660
But I...

04:25.280 --> 04:29.610
no, we want you to be a part of Clover.

04:29.610 --> 04:32.190
A member of our family, in other words.

04:33.060 --> 04:35.220
You can make the decision for yourself.

04:35.220 --> 04:38.410
Whatever you choose,
I'll respect your wishes.

04:38.410 --> 04:39.570
I...

04:39.570 --> 04:40.190
Yes?

04:40.820 --> 04:43.710
I want to stay with you and the others!

04:44.090 --> 04:46.580
Clover will take Rune in
as one of our own.

04:46.960 --> 04:48.160
Very well.

04:48.160 --> 04:50.310
But if you ever run into trouble,

04:50.310 --> 04:54.230
feel free to come see me
at the academy anytime.

04:54.230 --> 04:55.160
I will.

04:55.160 --> 04:57.720
So when are you heading back to Finis?

04:58.080 --> 04:59.460
Well...

04:59.460 --> 05:03.720
We plan to make preparations and thank
everyone who has helped us first,

05:03.720 --> 05:06.010
then begin our trip home in three days.

05:06.010 --> 05:10.900
We are especially grateful to
everyone in Scordia and Carmine.

05:11.200 --> 05:13.300
There's still much
we could learn from them.

05:13.300 --> 05:16.340
We hope to have a chance to thank them
and talk with them for a while.

05:16.340 --> 05:18.410
I'm afraid I have bad news, then.

05:18.750 --> 05:23.290
Both Scordia and Carmine have already
set off to undertake new missions.

05:23.580 --> 05:26.310
They have? That's a shame.

05:26.310 --> 05:28.420
We didn't get to thank them properly.

05:28.790 --> 05:34.110
They made even more of a name for themselves
after this Glad Shi-im business, after all.

05:34.110 --> 05:36.150
So long as you remain adventurers,

05:36.150 --> 05:38.300
you'll surely encounter them again.

05:38.740 --> 05:40.200
You're right.

05:40.200 --> 05:44.170
We need to make sure Clover
keeps growing until then, too.

05:44.170 --> 05:45.820
Yes, Master.

05:45.820 --> 05:48.310
We don't want to embarrass
ourselves when we see them.

05:48.850 --> 05:53.440
Well, Bodeman and I will be
heading back to Finis first.

05:53.440 --> 05:54.570
See you again.

05:54.950 --> 05:56.860
Thank you, truly, for all you've done.

05:57.320 --> 05:59.570
You have indeed saved this world,

05:59.980 --> 06:02.510
Hero Yuke Feldio.

06:05.800 --> 06:09.260
Thank you so much for all
you've done, as well.

06:14.330 --> 06:17.010
And now our quest is truly complete.

06:17.010 --> 06:18.970
Yes. You've earned some rest.

06:19.320 --> 06:21.260
Same to you.

06:21.260 --> 06:23.280
Guess we're shopping tomorrow, huh?

06:23.280 --> 06:27.100
You don't need to come
along with us, you know.

06:27.950 --> 06:30.480
Why not? You'll need someone
to help carry things.

06:30.840 --> 06:33.800
Marina, Rain, and Rune will help me.

06:33.800 --> 06:35.110
No need to worry.

06:35.110 --> 06:38.010
What about Nene? She's not going with you?

06:38.010 --> 06:41.610
Master, did you forget?
In Vordan Castle...

06:42.990 --> 06:47.600
There's no room left for me to hug you,
so I'll head back and wait.

06:47.600 --> 06:51.750
But... when you get back,
I demand a day of Nene time!

06:52.970 --> 06:55.560
Nene has been waiting eagerly for her day.

06:55.560 --> 06:58.100
Please invite her out.

06:58.100 --> 06:59.260
Okay, got it.

06:59.260 --> 07:03.370
But what am I supposed to
do for this "Nene time"?

07:03.370 --> 07:05.010
Anything is fine.

07:05.290 --> 07:08.740
As long as she's having fun with you.

07:09.670 --> 07:11.240
Is that how it works?

07:11.240 --> 07:12.770
Yes, it is.

07:13.180 --> 07:16.270
But her getting a day alone with you...

07:16.800 --> 07:20.030
If only I'd refrained
from hugging you that day,

07:20.880 --> 07:24.370
maybe I could have
demanded some Silk time...

07:24.370 --> 07:24.780
Huh?

07:25.660 --> 07:27.920
N-Nothing!

07:34.270 --> 07:36.420
I guess I shouldn't overthink it.

07:38.190 --> 07:39.170
Come in!

07:40.390 --> 07:42.300
Did you need something?

07:42.300 --> 07:43.310
Nene.

07:43.310 --> 07:44.160
Yes?!

07:44.160 --> 07:47.320
Y-Yuke, it's you! What brings you here?

07:47.320 --> 07:49.180
You're packing already?

07:49.550 --> 07:52.080
I'm not very good at keeping things tidy,

07:52.080 --> 07:54.290
so I thought I should start early.

07:54.290 --> 07:55.690
That's the spirit.

07:56.530 --> 07:57.990
So, um...

07:58.900 --> 07:59.570
Nene.

08:00.020 --> 08:00.830
Yes?

08:00.830 --> 08:01.940
About tomorrow...

08:04.040 --> 08:07.020
Think about what you'd like to do, okay?

08:07.020 --> 08:09.770
Let's forget everything and let loose.

08:09.770 --> 08:12.420
For, uh... Nene time, I mean.

08:16.180 --> 08:17.860
Well, goodnight.

08:34.990 --> 08:36.060
Yuke?

08:37.800 --> 08:39.400
Yuke!

08:39.710 --> 08:42.970
Stop that! You were lost in
thought again, weren't you?

08:42.970 --> 08:45.520
There's just been way too much happening.

08:45.520 --> 08:47.620
I can't stop myself, I guess.

08:48.040 --> 08:50.120
You're such a workaholic!

08:50.120 --> 08:54.370
You're the one who said we should
forget everything and let loose!

08:54.640 --> 08:56.880
Yeah. Sorry, Nene.

08:56.880 --> 08:59.380
It's okay. But...

08:59.380 --> 09:01.380
Today is Nene time,

09:01.690 --> 09:04.380
so I'm gonna make all
kinds of selfish demands!

09:08.610 --> 09:10.010
Go easy on me, okay?

09:13.200 --> 09:17.020
Nothing beats some good
grape wine in the sunshine.

09:17.360 --> 09:18.850
Since we came to Duna...

09:18.850 --> 09:23.250
No, even before that,
I haven't done anything like this.

09:23.250 --> 09:24.530
Really?

09:24.530 --> 09:28.530
I haven't done much drinking
since my time in Thunder Pike.

09:28.960 --> 09:30.820
Maybe I could only think of alcohol as

09:30.820 --> 09:33.700
something to enjoy the night
after completing an adventure.

09:37.160 --> 09:38.270
Good stuff.

09:38.270 --> 09:39.380
Isn't it?

09:40.640 --> 09:41.920
So... what are we doing?

09:42.640 --> 09:44.820
There are lots of things I want to do,

09:44.820 --> 09:47.400
but first, I'd like to go to the bazaar!

09:47.400 --> 09:49.900
Aren't Silk and the others already there?

09:49.900 --> 09:52.180
I don't mean the one for adventurers.

09:52.480 --> 09:55.530
Ah, I get it. We haven't been
to the other one.

09:55.530 --> 09:59.310
It sells all kinds of things from
Salmutaria and other countries, right?

09:59.660 --> 10:02.710
I'm sure none of it would be
of any use in adventuring,

10:02.710 --> 10:04.200
but I wanna check it out!

10:04.200 --> 10:05.940
Okay, then.

10:05.940 --> 10:07.850
Let's treat ourselves to some shopping.

10:07.850 --> 10:09.700
Yay!

10:19.470 --> 10:20.840
Used to that?

10:20.840 --> 10:22.720
No, not at all.

10:22.720 --> 10:28.470
Right. For a guy who can do anything,
you sure are hopeless with girls.

10:28.860 --> 10:33.220
I'm a jack of all trades and master of none.
There's plenty I haven't experienced.

10:33.590 --> 10:37.980
I don't know how to have
a date with a cute girl.

10:39.870 --> 10:42.140
The way you do it so naturally
is just mean.

10:42.140 --> 10:42.610
Huh?

10:42.960 --> 10:45.060
Nothing. Never mind.

10:45.770 --> 10:47.360
Oh, there's the bazaar!

10:51.860 --> 10:55.240
Look! Those tunics are see-through!

10:55.240 --> 10:57.750
Are those earrings coral?

10:57.750 --> 11:02.000
Are those cosmetics made
with Layahiman rock salt?!

11:02.000 --> 11:05.000
There are so many things
I've never seen before!

11:05.250 --> 11:06.500
This way!

11:07.320 --> 11:08.880
And now this way!

11:08.880 --> 11:09.340
Whoa!

11:09.340 --> 11:10.930
We're going over there, too!

11:12.970 --> 11:15.640
If you see anything you want,
I'll buy it for you.

11:15.640 --> 11:17.940
Oh, I couldn't make you do that.

11:17.940 --> 11:20.770
I'll pay for the things I want myself.

11:20.770 --> 11:24.090
You say that, but you
haven't bought anything.

11:24.090 --> 11:26.420
You're having trouble deciding, right?

11:28.260 --> 11:29.900
Consider it my thanks.

11:30.240 --> 11:34.240
I've put you through a lot
of trouble and worry lately.

11:34.240 --> 11:35.750
So don't hold back.

11:36.370 --> 11:37.790
You're sure?

11:37.790 --> 11:41.530
Of course. Today is a day
of Nene time, isn't it?

11:41.530 --> 11:44.920
Yeah, but... I can't figure it out myself.

11:45.290 --> 11:48.800
I don't mean just buying stuff.
You can be more selfish, you know.

11:49.150 --> 11:50.310
I can?

11:50.310 --> 11:54.180
Yeah. Just say whatever's on your mind.

11:54.710 --> 11:57.480
You should really learn
to be more selfish.

11:59.030 --> 12:01.730
Remember you said that!
I won't hold back now!

12:01.730 --> 12:03.140
Bring it on.

12:03.590 --> 12:06.310
Okay, then, we'll start with this shop!

12:06.310 --> 12:09.820
There are some other places I want
to visit after we buy stuff here!

12:09.820 --> 12:13.320
There's a lot I want to do, and
a lot I want you to do for me!

12:13.320 --> 12:16.160
Nene time isn't over until night falls!

12:16.160 --> 12:18.090
You'd better be ready!

12:23.330 --> 12:26.470
I really appreciate everything, Maniella.

12:26.470 --> 12:27.960
I should be thanking you.

12:28.300 --> 12:31.410
You, too, Fina. You took
very good care of us.

12:31.410 --> 12:32.590
Thank you.

12:32.920 --> 12:34.630
It's been fun.

12:34.630 --> 12:36.720
Please come visit again, okay?

12:37.100 --> 12:39.260
Yeah! We totally will!

12:39.260 --> 12:40.970
I want to get in the hot spring again.

12:41.320 --> 12:43.910
I love the hot spring, too!

12:43.910 --> 12:45.850
Yeah, it felt great!

12:46.130 --> 12:49.180
Yes. I wish we could take it home with us!

12:49.180 --> 12:51.700
I don't think that would work very well...

12:51.700 --> 12:53.610
But we should come again.

12:53.960 --> 12:54.990
Yeah!

12:55.880 --> 13:00.490
Well, thank you again for
all you've done for us.

13:00.490 --> 13:02.240
Thank you!

13:06.250 --> 13:09.380
Well, let's go back to Finis...

13:09.380 --> 13:10.970
and to our home!

13:17.010 --> 13:18.660
You hold this here...

13:18.660 --> 13:19.760
Uh-huh.

13:35.460 --> 13:37.150
We're finally back!

13:37.420 --> 13:40.210
Good old Finis!

13:45.000 --> 13:46.910
What a pretty town!

13:47.290 --> 13:50.120
You'll be living here from today on, too.

13:50.120 --> 13:51.010
Yeah!

13:51.010 --> 13:52.920
Isn't that Marina?

13:52.920 --> 13:55.720
It is! Clover is back!

13:55.720 --> 13:57.420
Hey! Welcome back!

13:59.430 --> 14:00.520
Clover!

14:00.520 --> 14:02.010
I watched your streams!

14:02.010 --> 14:04.030
I'm so glad you're back safe and sound!

14:04.030 --> 14:04.930
Welcome back!

14:05.240 --> 14:07.070
What is all this?

14:07.070 --> 14:11.020
They're celebrating our return home!

14:11.640 --> 14:12.940
Hey!

14:13.320 --> 14:15.910
I had no idea it would be like this.

14:15.910 --> 14:19.050
I'm surprised... but also happy.

14:19.050 --> 14:22.320
They were all watching our
streams and cheering us on.

14:22.580 --> 14:24.740
It really feels like we
accomplished something.

14:24.740 --> 14:26.450
I kinda feel like I could cry!

14:26.450 --> 14:29.210
Thank you, everyone!

14:29.210 --> 14:32.650
Clover is back! We're home!

14:32.650 --> 14:34.960
Welcome back!

14:35.590 --> 14:37.840
I'm going to report to Benwood.

14:37.840 --> 14:39.970
You guys can go home ahead of me.

14:40.310 --> 14:41.490
Got it!

14:43.340 --> 14:45.300
Welcome back, Yuke.

14:45.300 --> 14:47.350
You've had a very long journey.

14:47.770 --> 14:50.850
We just got back in from Duna, Mamar.

14:51.250 --> 14:55.610
I have many questions I'd like to ask,
but I'll save them for another day.

14:55.610 --> 14:57.860
Thanks for helping us out
with Rain's troubles.

14:59.050 --> 15:03.870
The investigations into Count Crowder,
the falsified family register, and—

15:04.150 --> 15:06.840
You don't know who might be listening.

15:06.840 --> 15:10.250
Don't say too much. It's too important.

15:10.750 --> 15:11.940
Right...

15:11.940 --> 15:14.000
Still, thank you.

15:14.330 --> 15:15.570
Not at all.

15:15.570 --> 15:19.160
But I wonder, how do you intend
to repay this debt to me?

15:19.160 --> 15:20.630
I look forward to finding out.

15:20.630 --> 15:21.720
Er...

15:25.230 --> 15:27.260
So that's the whole story.

15:27.630 --> 15:31.670
Right. I heard most of it
from the old woman.

15:31.670 --> 15:32.890
Old woman?

15:32.890 --> 15:34.310
Maniella.

15:34.310 --> 15:35.520
You call her that?

15:36.010 --> 15:39.780
Anyway, you should have also received
a report about Prince Mastoma.

15:39.780 --> 15:41.430
I have.

15:41.430 --> 15:44.090
We've already begun to take action,

15:44.090 --> 15:47.660
but I can't promise there'll
be much we can do right away.

15:47.660 --> 15:50.530
Just sit tight and be patient for a bit.

15:50.530 --> 15:51.270
Okay.

15:51.270 --> 15:53.920
As for your reward for this mission...

15:54.290 --> 15:56.970
I'll deposit it in Clover's account later.

15:56.970 --> 15:58.800
Deposit it? Why?

15:59.220 --> 16:02.310
Because it's too much
to hand over in cash.

16:02.310 --> 16:03.180
It's that much?

16:03.180 --> 16:05.020
Of course it is.

16:05.020 --> 16:09.540
It was a quest straight from
the kingdom, and you nailed it.

16:09.540 --> 16:12.060
Don't faint when you see
the amount, you hear?

16:12.060 --> 16:15.380
I'll try not to get my hopes up.

16:16.100 --> 16:18.160
Did I hear that Yuke is back?!

16:18.160 --> 16:19.160
Yuke?

16:19.160 --> 16:20.320
I'm back, Jamie.

16:20.960 --> 16:23.860
Are you all right?
You're not hurt, are you?

16:23.860 --> 16:25.070
No pain anywhere?

16:25.070 --> 16:27.080
C-Come on, Jamie...

16:27.080 --> 16:33.460
She was inconsolable when she heard
you'd disappeared in Glad Shi-im.

16:33.870 --> 16:34.710
Huh?

16:34.710 --> 16:38.860
She kept insisting, "I'm going to Duna!
I have to save him!"

16:38.860 --> 16:41.020
It was all I could do to calm her down.

16:41.020 --> 16:43.470
I kept telling her you,
of all people, would be fine.

16:43.470 --> 16:46.000
But she was so worried,
she actually cried.

16:46.000 --> 16:47.300
Guild Master, please!

16:47.680 --> 16:50.740
Sorry about that. Thanks, Jamie!

16:50.740 --> 16:53.400
I-I didn't cry, okay?!

16:53.400 --> 16:56.690
But you did worry about me, right?
That makes me happy.

16:57.050 --> 17:02.440
I was only worried about what happened
if I couldn't get Tec's medicine anymore!

17:03.400 --> 17:05.320
Just can't be honest, can you?

17:05.320 --> 17:08.500
It's obvious that I'd worry
about my leader!

17:08.500 --> 17:11.200
I'm a part of Clover, after all.

17:11.200 --> 17:12.130
Yep.

17:12.600 --> 17:18.860
She said, "When I can start adventuring
again, I'll be the one to save Yuke!"

17:18.860 --> 17:20.230
Guild Master!

17:20.230 --> 17:23.140
Well, you never told me
to keep it a secret.

17:28.550 --> 17:32.350
Oh, right. Yuke, about Clover's base...

17:32.350 --> 17:35.810
I took care of it with the real estate agent,
Mr. Monday, while you were away.

17:36.130 --> 17:39.920
It's clean, and there's enough
food to hold you for a while, too.

17:39.920 --> 17:41.650
I can always count on you.

17:42.010 --> 17:44.360
Be sure to rest when you get back.

17:44.360 --> 17:45.110
I will.

17:45.110 --> 17:47.780
Let's have a party
soon to celebrate our return.

17:48.130 --> 17:49.560
With you, of course.

17:50.460 --> 17:51.280
Okay!

17:51.570 --> 17:54.500
You guys sure do like parties, huh?

17:54.500 --> 17:56.290
Well, you don't have to come.

17:56.290 --> 17:57.790
Oh, I'm going.

17:57.790 --> 18:00.060
I wouldn't miss out on free booze!

18:04.600 --> 18:09.050
I remodeled the small room upstairs
a bit with Jamie's counsel.

18:09.450 --> 18:12.090
I wanted to make it comfortable
for Niberune.

18:12.090 --> 18:13.320
Isn't that cool?

18:13.320 --> 18:14.930
Yeah! My own room!

18:14.930 --> 18:19.480
Also, the door to the bathroom
was a bit loose, so I fixed it.

18:19.480 --> 18:21.560
I found no other problems.

18:21.560 --> 18:26.190
Once again, I'm so glad you
all made it back safely.

18:26.190 --> 18:28.740
Please get some good rest.

18:28.740 --> 18:32.070
Thank you for tending to the place
while we were away, Mr. Monday.

18:32.360 --> 18:33.720
Yeah! Thanks a lot!

18:33.720 --> 18:34.950
Thank you.

18:34.950 --> 18:36.940
Well, I'll be on my way.

18:40.660 --> 18:43.380
So this is where I'll be living
from now on!

18:44.050 --> 18:45.210
That's right!

18:45.210 --> 18:47.100
We can take baths together!

18:47.100 --> 18:48.280
I'd love to!

18:48.280 --> 18:49.380
I'm back.

18:49.380 --> 18:50.760
You'd love to what?

18:51.420 --> 18:52.260
Take baths!

18:52.260 --> 18:54.010
Do you want to get in with us, too?

18:55.470 --> 18:57.870
Come on, stop teasing me!

18:57.870 --> 18:59.390
Guys, do you have a minute?

18:59.640 --> 19:00.550
Sure.

19:00.550 --> 19:02.880
You all did great on the mission.

19:02.880 --> 19:07.070
I think we should take some days off
to rest before making new plans.

19:07.070 --> 19:08.120
Agreed.

19:08.120 --> 19:11.280
But you're the one who
resists resting the most.

19:11.960 --> 19:14.170
You're the one who'd better rest!

19:14.170 --> 19:14.890
Yeah.

19:14.890 --> 19:16.290
I know, I know.

19:16.290 --> 19:18.240
I wonder about that.

19:18.240 --> 19:22.520
Rune, let's keep an eye on Yuke
to make sure he rests, okay?

19:22.520 --> 19:23.340
Yeah!

19:24.540 --> 19:28.300
Hey, wasn't Scordia
doing their stream today?

19:28.300 --> 19:31.010
Yeah! Let's fire up the tablet!

19:31.010 --> 19:32.180
I wanna watch, too!

19:32.450 --> 19:35.670
Hold it, Marina, Nene, and Rune.

19:35.670 --> 19:37.770
Save it for after you finish unpacking.

19:37.770 --> 19:38.910
We'll do that later!

19:38.910 --> 19:39.560
Yeah!

19:39.920 --> 19:41.450
Just a little peek?

19:43.610 --> 19:46.020
Oh, all right. Just for a little bit.

19:46.020 --> 19:47.940
Awesome! Thanks, Silk!

19:47.940 --> 19:49.240
Thanks!

19:49.240 --> 19:49.740
Yeah!

19:50.110 --> 19:51.070
- Honestly, you girls...

19:51.070 --> 19:52.000
- I can't wait!
- Honestly, you girls...

19:52.000 --> 19:52.490
- I can't wait!
- But to be honest, I'm curious about it, too.

19:52.490 --> 19:55.330
- Rune, do you know Sho and Gato?
- But to be honest, I'm curious about it, too.

20:01.100 --> 20:02.250
Yuke?

20:03.320 --> 20:05.750
You look lost in thought again.

20:06.070 --> 20:07.930
Huh? I do?

20:07.930 --> 20:11.160
I just couldn't help thinking
about what we'll do next.

20:11.160 --> 20:14.490
This is why you need to be watched.

20:14.490 --> 20:17.390
You just told us earlier we should rest.

20:17.390 --> 20:18.510
Yeah, I know.

20:20.620 --> 20:22.910
Hey, Yuke?

20:25.140 --> 20:26.730
You're amazing.

20:28.190 --> 20:31.180
You've helped all of us out so much.

20:31.180 --> 20:34.860
Just having you around makes
me feel like I can do anything.

20:35.490 --> 20:36.930
Really?

20:36.930 --> 20:40.910
I think I'm the one getting all
the help from you guys, though.

20:40.910 --> 20:42.250
It's okay.

20:42.660 --> 20:44.500
Just keep being who you are.

20:46.730 --> 20:49.060
There's that look again.

20:51.960 --> 20:56.240
Yuke, let's drink tonight and
stop thinking about everything.

20:56.240 --> 20:58.260
Good idea. Until we're dead drunk!

20:59.330 --> 21:00.260
Don't worry.

21:00.610 --> 21:04.020
If you do get wasted,
I'll stay with you until morning.

21:05.030 --> 21:06.520
Okay, Rain.

21:07.520 --> 21:08.980
So let's go.

21:09.670 --> 21:10.230
Yeah.

21:10.230 --> 21:12.430
Yuke, you're late!

21:12.430 --> 21:13.670
- Took you long enough!
- Sorry about that.

21:13.670 --> 21:14.890
I'm starving!

21:14.890 --> 21:15.810
Sorry.

21:15.810 --> 21:17.700
The usual, please, Master!

21:17.700 --> 21:18.530
Okay...

21:18.840 --> 21:20.230
To Clover!

21:20.230 --> 21:21.840
Cheers!

22:56.050 --> 22:56.780
(King's Order)

22:56.780 --> 22:59.330
(King's Order)
Next time, "King's Order."

22:59.330 --> 23:01.050
(King's Order)
